course: dictionary
lesson: 2155
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the words around it show which meaning the writer means. The word core is a good example. «The outer core is liquid iron and nickel» uses core for the deep centre of the Earth, not for an apple.
explain: Look for clues. «Skaters balance using the inner ear, eyes and strong leg and core muscles» is about the body, because balance and muscles are the clues. Ask yourself: what meaning would fit here? Then try that meaning in the sentence.
explain: Your meaning must make sense in the whole sentence. In «core subjects», core means most important, so English, maths and science are the main subjects at school.
fact: Some words have more than one meaning. Context tells you which meaning the writer means.
fact: «Core» can be a noun, an adjective or a verb.
fact: The core of an apple is the hard middle part with the seeds.
fact: The core of the Earth is its very hot centre, and the inner core is solid.
fact: «Core» as an adjective means most important or central, as in core subjects.
exercise: «Skaters balance using strong leg and core muscles.» What does core mean here? | The middle of an apple | The sharp edge of a skate | *The muscles around your tummy and back | The hottest place in the Earth
exercise: «The outer core is liquid iron and nickel.» What is the outer core? | *A layer of liquid metal deep inside the Earth | A layer of ice on top of the sea | The hard middle of a pear | A solid rock on the Moon
exercise: Ben reads that English, maths and science are core subjects. What does core mean? | Hot and dry | Hard and sour | Small and hidden | *Most important or main
test: Ella needs to core the apples before she bakes them. What does core mean here? | *To take out the hard middle part | To polish until they shine | To eat them whole | To put them in the fridge
test: «The core of the problem is that we have no time.» What does core mean here? | The strongest muscle | *The most important part | The hottest place | The soft fruit inside
exam: «The inner core is a solid ball of iron and nickel, and it stays solid despite the heat because the enormous pressure above squeezes it.» Why does the inner core stay solid? | Because it is very cold | *Because the enormous pressure above squeezes it | Because it is outside the Earth | Because it is made of water
